@externalUrl = http://localhost:5007
@internalUrl = http://localhost:5099
@externalApiKey = development-external-key
@internalBearerToken = <entra-access-token>

### External API - list public animal profiles (API key required)
GET {{externalUrl}}/api/external/animals
X-API-Key: {{externalApiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### External API - missing API key
GET {{externalUrl}}/api/external/animals
Accept: application/json

### Internal API - list registry records (bearer required)
GET {{internalUrl}}/api/internal/animals
Authorization: Bearer {{internalBearerToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Internal API - create animal in the internal API's in-memory dataset (bearer required)
POST {{internalUrl}}/api/internal/animals
Authorization: Bearer {{internalBearerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "registeredName": "Luna",
  "species": "Canis lupus familiaris",
  "category": "Mammal",
  "breed": "Mixed",
  "birthDate": null,
  "publicDescription": "Friendly dog looking for a home.",
  "availableForAdoption": true,
  "attributes": {
    "habitat": "Home"
  },
  "medicalNotes": "Routine check-up up to date"
}

### External API - list public profiles from the external API's in-memory dataset
GET {{externalUrl}}/api/external/animals
X-API-Key: {{externalApiKey}}
Accept: application/json
